[
    {
        "content": "<p>I have been playing around with <code>bi/monpred.v</code> and is trying to port it.</p>\n<p>In Lean, <code>MonPred</code> is defined as follow:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonPred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BIIndex</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">BI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">holds</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">mono</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"o\">},</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I.rel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">holds</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">holds</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>where <code>BIIndex</code> is a structure of indices, with a preorder relation:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BIIndex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Relation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rel_preorder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Preorder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rel</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>With <code>MonPred</code>, I defined <code>sForall</code> and <code>sExists</code>. Here, let's focus on <code>sForall</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sForall</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Ψ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonPred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonPred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">holds</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iprop</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⌜</span><span class=\"n\">Ψ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">⌝</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">mono</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h_rel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">forall_mono</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">imp_mono_r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P.mono</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h_rel</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This definition is similar to the definition of <code>sForall</code> on <code>SiProp</code> but uses <code>PROP</code> instead of <code>Prop</code>.</p>\n<p>I tried to define a <code>BI</code> instance for <code>MonPred I PROP</code>, but then I got stuck trying to prove <code>sForall_ne</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Ψ₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ψ₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonPred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n<span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">liftRel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≡</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"bp\">≡</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ψ₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ψ₂</span>\n<span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I.type</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">BI.sForall</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ψ₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">holds</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≡</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"bp\">≡</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">BI.sForall</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ψ₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">holds</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Here, I destruct <code>h</code> and then use <code>forall_ne</code> on the underlying <code>PROP</code>, that leads to:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Ψ₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ψ₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonPred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n<span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I.type</span>\n<span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonPred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ψ₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ψ₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≡</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"bp\">≡</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n<span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonPred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ψ₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ψ₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≡</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"bp\">≡</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n<span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonPred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iprop</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⌜</span><span class=\"n\">Ψ₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">⌝</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P.holds</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≡</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"bp\">≡</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iprop</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⌜</span><span class=\"n\">Ψ₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">⌝</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P.holds</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>At this step, I got stuck.</p>\n<p>Analyze the proof of <code>sForall_ne</code> on <code>SiProp</code>, I observe that, on <code>SiProp</code> we can unfold <code>≡{n}≡</code> to <code>⊢</code>, and then we can introduce <code>Ψ₁ P</code> and use <code>h₁</code> and so on. However, in the case of <code>MonPred</code>, <code>≡{n}≡</code> is abstract and is completely unrelated to <code>⊢</code>, and we cannot use the same strategy.</p>\n<p>I am wondering whether my current definition of <code>sForall</code> is problematic and there is a better definition, or the problem lies somewhere else?</p>",
        "id": 592891860,
        "sender_full_name": "Viet Anh Nguyen",
        "timestamp": 1777956314
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Can you make progress with applying <code>imp_ne</code>?</p>",
        "id": 592936392,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Sammler",
        "timestamp": 1777969401
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, I tried that, I should have mentioned what would happen. After applying <code>imp_ne</code>, we need to prove:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><code>iprop(⌜Ψ₁ P⌝) ≡{n}≡ iprop(⌜Ψ₂ P⌝)</code></li>\n<li><code>P.holds i ≡{n}≡ P.holds i</code>, this is easy</li>\n</ol>\n<p>For <code>iprop(⌜Ψ₁ P⌝) ≡{n}≡ iprop(⌜Ψ₂ P⌝)</code>, we may something similar to <code>SIProp.pure_dist_of_iff</code> to progress:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure_dist_of_iff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ψ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ψ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≡</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"bp\">≡</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ψ</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>but at the moment we don't have that, and I doubt whether we can have that.</p>\n<p>Assume that we manage to find and prove such a statement, we can then turn the goal into <code>Ψ₁ P ↔ Ψ₂ P</code>. Now, if this can be proven, the proof should use <code>h₁</code> and <code>h₂</code>, but it doesn't seem like <code>h₁</code> and <code>h₂</code> can get us through here.</p>",
        "id": 592943850,
        "sender_full_name": "Viet Anh Nguyen",
        "timestamp": 1777971364
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This seems indeed a bit tricky. I am also not sure how to best approach this. (I think you can prove <code>pure_dist_of_iff</code> using classical reasoning, but I don't see how this statement helps you for the reasons you mention.)</p>",
        "id": 592968269,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Sammler",
        "timestamp": 1777978398
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"1066222\">@Viet Anh Nguyen</span> Did you ever manage to solve this problem?</p>",
        "id": 599193988,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Sammler",
        "timestamp": 1780328769
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi there, sorry for the late reply (just come back from a vacation). I wasn’t able to come up with a solution.</p>\n<p>I thought about tweaking some definitions, but I haven’t gotten to the bottom of it yet. And also, I’m worried it might break other parts of the project, and I’m not even sure if changing the definition makes sense.</p>",
        "id": 599754420,
        "sender_full_name": "Viet Anh Nguyen",
        "timestamp": 1780482277
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I tried looking at it again with a fresh mind and some help from agents. After a morning of back-and-forth, the key turned out to be a \"Eureka\" lemma about <code>sForall</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Ψ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonPred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonPred</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sForall</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ψ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊣⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BI</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sForall</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ψ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>With this lemma, we can rewrite both sides to <code>BI.sForall</code>, after which the proof follows from <code>BI.sForall_ne</code>. Ditto for <code>sExists</code>.</p>\n<p>I don't fully understand the proofs yet, though. I guess I'll spend some time trying to understand them.</p>",
        "id": 600018290,
        "sender_full_name": "Viet Anh Nguyen",
        "timestamp": 1780557742
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I also don't fully understand how this works, but this is great news <span aria-label=\"tada\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f389\" role=\"img\" title=\"tada\">:tada:</span> Thanks for looking into this again!</p>",
        "id": 600030583,
